00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:06.540
And Mike Schur actually said that the gifts were incredibly hard to manage.

777
00:30:06.900 --> 00:30:11.520
Because they start off as Secret Santa, so everybody had a person that they bought a specific

778
00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:12.140
gift for.

779
00:30:12.140 --> 00:30:16.480
And then you had to track the gifts as they went around in the Yankee swap.

780
00:30:16.760 --> 00:30:23.960
He actually, in the script of this episode, there is a whole page where he lists the gifts.

781
00:30:24.200 --> 00:30:25.760
Who bought who what?

782
00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:29.420
And he did this for Veda, our script supervisor.

783
00:30:29.740 --> 00:30:36.020
We haven't really talked about her, but Veda's job is to sit and watch every take that is filmed

784
00:30:36.020 --> 00:30:40.020
and make notes about everything that happens continuity-wise.

785
00:30:40.580 --> 00:30:42.380
So, I mean, like, really specific.

786
00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:48.540
So, like, if in a scene you take a drink of your tea on a certain line and then scratch your nose

787
00:30:48.540 --> 00:30:53.860
on another one, Veda writes it down so that you do it the same every time for editing purposes.

788
00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:54.320
Yeah.

789
00:30:54.520 --> 00:31:00.400
Veda would come up to us and say, Angela, you were holding that pen in your left hand in the first

790
00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:00.760
take.

791
00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:03.700
And in the second take, you picked it up and held it in your right hand.

792
00:31:03.700 --> 00:31:05.400
So, that's not going to match.

793
00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:09.020
So, you need to pick which hand you're going to hold that pen in and do it in every take the same

794
00:31:09.020 --> 00:31:09.220
way.

795
00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:09.700
Yeah.

796
00:31:09.900 --> 00:31:14.080
Because otherwise, when you edit it together, the pen is magically bouncing from hand to hand.

797
00:31:14.880 --> 00:31:19.800
So, Mike was really worried about Veda in this episode.

798
00:31:20.560 --> 00:31:23.340
And so, he made this list just for Veda.

799
00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:25.060
And I have it from the script.

800
00:31:25.320 --> 00:31:26.280
Oh, fantastic.

801
00:31:26.500 --> 00:31:26.900
Okay.

802
00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:30.600
So, this is what everyone was intended to give.

803
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:32.480
And we got a lot of fan questions about this.

804
00:31:32.480 --> 00:31:37.040
Like, a lot of people wrote in and said, you know, eventually Michael's going to get the

805
00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:38.500
paintball lessons from Dwight.

806
00:31:38.640 --> 00:31:41.340
But they're like, who did Dwight intend that to go to?

807
00:31:41.560 --> 00:31:43.280
So, I have all the answers right here.

808
00:31:43.280 --> 00:31:43.700
Are you ready?

809
00:31:43.900 --> 00:31:44.160
Yeah.

810
00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:44.940
Okay.

811
00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:49.580
Dwight got Phyllis the paintball lessons and the pellets.

812
00:31:49.580 --> 00:31:51.220
That was his gift to Phyllis.

813
00:31:51.900 --> 00:31:53.920
Phyllis made Michael an oven mitt.

814
00:31:54.800 --> 00:31:56.680
Michael got Ryan an iPod.

815
00:31:56.680 --> 00:32:02.640
Ryan got Toby a book of short stories by George Saunders, who happens to be one of Mike Schur's favorite writers.

816
00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:05.080
Toby got Angela the baby poster.

817
00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:07.660
Angela bought Stanley a picture frame.

818
00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:10.440
Stanley got Kelly a nameplate.

819
00:32:10.980 --> 00:32:13.080
Kelly got Oscar a shower radio.

820
00:32:13.620 --> 00:32:16.060
Oscar got Creed a shamrock keychain.

821
00:32:16.600 --> 00:32:19.120
Creed got Jim one of his own shirts.

822
00:32:19.880 --> 00:32:21.560
Jim got Pam the teapot.

823
00:32:21.700 --> 00:32:23.500
And this is something that got cut out.

824
00:32:23.780 --> 00:32:26.520
Pam made Meredith a drawing of The Office.

825
00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:28.580
I read about that online.

826
00:32:28.940 --> 00:32:29.180
Yeah.

827
00:32:29.300 --> 00:32:30.540
And there was this big thing.

828
00:32:30.760 --> 00:32:32.080
It's in the deleted scenes.

829
00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:33.860
This is something I have to tell you.

830
00:32:33.980 --> 00:32:35.960
I got a DVD player for Christmas.

831
00:32:36.320 --> 00:32:36.660
What?

832
00:32:36.960 --> 00:32:39.060
My husband got me a DVD player.

833
00:32:39.240 --> 00:32:40.880
So, I got the CDs.

834
00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:42.460
He bought me the CD set.

835
00:32:42.640 --> 00:32:44.180
And I got a DVD player.

836
00:32:44.180 --> 00:32:47.160
And last night, I got to watch all the deleted scenes.

837
00:32:47.380 --> 00:32:49.600
Oh, Angela, you must be so happy.

838
00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:50.460
I was so happy.

839
00:32:50.460 --> 00:32:51.480
And there's so many.

840
00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:52.240
Oh, yeah.

841
00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:52.920
There's so many.

842
00:32:53.060 --> 00:32:56.940
For the Christmas episode, you guys, there are so many great deleted scenes.

843
00:32:57.080 --> 00:32:58.920
I don't want to get us off topic here.

844
00:32:59.300 --> 00:33:03.960
But there, in the deleted scenes, Meredith opens up her painting.

845
00:33:04.320 --> 00:33:05.400
That is from Pam.

846
00:33:05.520 --> 00:33:06.740
And it's a drawing of The Office.

847
00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:09.660
Well, there's a big backstory here.

848
00:33:09.820 --> 00:33:13.760
Again, with Phil, I don't do Pam's drawings.

849
00:33:13.760 --> 00:33:15.160
People ask me that all the time.

850
00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:16.720
I'm not an artiSt.

851
00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:21.360
I mean, we've talked about this, or have we, that I do cartoons.

852
00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:22.480
I do cartooning.

853
00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:23.940
She's very good at cartooning.

854
00:33:24.040 --> 00:33:25.900
And I have a few that you've drawn that I've saved.

855
00:33:26.080 --> 00:33:27.360
I think you're fantastic.

856
00:33:27.700 --> 00:33:29.740
Well, I love my little expressive cartoons.

857
00:33:29.940 --> 00:33:33.500
But I needed Pam and wanted Pam to be a better artist than I am.

858
00:33:34.220 --> 00:33:37.920
So, there is a young art student that does all of Pam's drawings.

859
00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:48.980
They went out to a bunch of people, like 12 different artists, to turn in samples to be the artist behind Pam.

860
00:33:49.180 --> 00:33:50.480
And they picked a young woman.

861
00:33:50.980 --> 00:33:53.320
Now, Jenna, I read, and you can tell me if this is true.

862
00:33:53.320 --> 00:34:05.600
I read that the first painting that they had for this episode to give to Meredith from Pam, that they had one of our set art people, who was a man, do it.

863
00:34:05.720 --> 00:34:05.900
Yeah.

864
00:34:06.080 --> 00:34:07.980
And when they looked at it, it looked too masculine.

865
00:34:08.200 --> 00:34:08.420
Yeah.

866
00:34:08.420 --> 00:34:10.760
And so, then they went out to female artists.

867
00:34:10.920 --> 00:34:11.400
That's true.

868
00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:12.780
To have a little bit of a softer touch.

869
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:13.140
Yeah.

870
00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.560
And there were something like 12 different artists who all submitted their work.

871
00:34:17.360 --> 00:34:18.680
And I wish I knew her name.

872
00:34:18.760 --> 00:34:19.720
Unfortunately, I don't.

873
00:34:19.840 --> 00:34:23.500
But maybe I can find that out and reveal that in a future episode.

874
00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:25.460
And then, so, finally, two more gifts.

875
00:34:25.600 --> 00:34:28.340
Meredith got Dwight some shot glasses from Cancun.

876
00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:30.560
And Kevin got himself a foot bath.

877
00:34:30.760 --> 00:34:36.360
Guys, around 5 minutes, 55 seconds, there is a scene where Michael is talking to Jim at Jim's desk.

878
00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:40.340
This is when he reveals that he got Ryan for Secret Santa.

879
00:34:40.980 --> 00:34:44.340
And I just want to say, you see a ton of background action.

880
00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:46.600
Angela, you're walking from reception.

881
00:34:47.160 --> 00:34:49.840
Over Steve's shoulder, you see Toby and Mindy talking.

882
00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:50.300
Yeah.

883
00:34:50.840 --> 00:34:53.320
They are 100% not in character.

884
00:34:53.540 --> 00:34:55.140
Not in character at all.

885
00:34:55.340 --> 00:34:56.080
I saw that, too.

886
00:34:56.160 --> 00:35:00.360
I was like, they're just talking about probably something in the writer's room or a story pitch.

887
00:35:00.420 --> 00:35:01.700
Or they're just having a conversation.

888
00:35:02.180 --> 00:35:02.400
Yeah.

889
00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:04.340
I mean, Paul is just being Paul.

890
00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:04.620
Yeah.

891
00:35:04.620 --> 00:35:09.140
If anyone's curious, the difference between Toby and Paul, go to 5 minutes, 55 seconds.

892
00:35:09.140 --> 00:35:11.640
And you can see Paul and Mindy having a conversation in the background.

893
00:35:11.760 --> 00:35:12.400
Yeah, exactly.

894
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:15.040
Tree lighting.

895
00:35:15.500 --> 00:35:15.900
Okay.

896
00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:17.400
I have been waiting for this moment.

897
00:35:17.440 --> 00:35:19.020
The Christmas tree lighting.

898
00:35:19.660 --> 00:35:23.900
This starts the beginning of Everyone Happy, Angela Pissed.

899
00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:29.520
So, this Christmas tree, the top of it has been hacked off by Kevin.

900
00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:33.260
It is covered in so much tinsel.

901
00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:33.700
Yeah.

902
00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:35.120
So much tinsel.

903
00:35:35.340 --> 00:35:37.900
It has a smattering of just blue and red ball ornaments.

904
00:35:37.900 --> 00:35:39.840
It's just not their best effort.

905
00:35:40.120 --> 00:35:45.040
And then it has the tiniest of tiny white lights, thanks to Phyllis.

906
00:35:45.180 --> 00:35:46.820
So, Dwight makes a big deal of it.

907
00:35:46.980 --> 00:35:50.700
He, like, takes the, like, the outlet, like the plug.

908
00:35:50.860 --> 00:35:51.460
What do you call it?

909
00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:52.680
The plug?

910
00:35:52.800 --> 00:35:53.320
The plug.

911
00:35:53.320 --> 00:35:55.000
Like, he takes the plug from Stanley.

912
00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:56.000
He wants to plug it in.

913
00:35:56.040 --> 00:35:57.260
He's like, just like Rockefeller Center.

914
00:35:57.580 --> 00:36:00.880
And everyone gathers around and is like, brr, brr.

915
00:36:01.340 --> 00:36:03.200
And Phyllis is like, I'm sorry.

916
00:36:03.520 --> 00:36:09.280
And at 6 minutes, 38 seconds, you see my first pissed off face.

917
00:36:09.440 --> 00:36:10.980
Like, dang it, Phyllis.

918
00:36:11.200 --> 00:36:14.740
It's also one of those moments where I feel like Angela is like, I knew it.

919
00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:15.400
I knew it.

920
00:36:15.400 --> 00:36:17.860
I knew I couldn't trust her to do these lights.

921
00:36:17.920 --> 00:36:20.120
Why do I even have her do anything?

922
00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:20.300
Ever.

923
00:36:20.300 --> 00:36:21.620
Why do you have anyone do anything?

924
00:36:21.680 --> 00:36:21.960
Yeah.

925
00:36:23.320 --> 00:36:24.500
You can't let anyone do anything.

926
00:36:24.700 --> 00:36:25.620
These people are worthless.

927
00:36:25.940 --> 00:36:26.240
Exactly.

928
00:36:26.960 --> 00:36:31.600
You know, that Christmas tree light thing is based on a real thing from Mike Schur's life.

929
00:36:31.880 --> 00:36:32.580
I know.

930
00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:38.660
He said that when he and his wife got their first tree in New York, he bought a bunch of

931
00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:41.100
small lights for the tree, and he wrapped them around.

932
00:36:41.220 --> 00:36:43.120
And when he plugged it in, you couldn't really see them.

933
00:36:44.900 --> 00:36:45.860
I love that.

934
00:36:46.020 --> 00:36:49.640
I love when writers work those little moments from their real life into the show.

935
00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:53.960
So I thought, speaking about people who are acting like themselves instead of their characters,

936
00:36:54.220 --> 00:36:57.740
I thought Jim's talking head about Creed's gift is so John.

937
00:36:58.040 --> 00:36:58.780
It is John.

938
00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:00.460
That is John right there.

939
00:37:00.600 --> 00:37:00.760
Yeah.

940
00:37:01.060 --> 00:37:04.480
All the delivery, the smile, all of it.

941
00:37:04.700 --> 00:37:07.460
And then, of course, Creed's talking head made me laugh so hard.

942
00:37:07.700 --> 00:37:09.780
Creed is very funny in this episode.

943
00:37:09.940 --> 00:37:14.980
I mean, everybody has some great moments, but Creed cracked me up a bunch in this episode.

944
00:37:14.980 --> 00:37:16.940
So now Secret Santa is starting.

945
00:37:17.180 --> 00:37:17.340
Yep.

946
00:37:17.660 --> 00:37:20.360
And everyone is gathered around in some office chairs.

947
00:37:20.620 --> 00:37:26.300
And I want to say, truly, I know we were joking about Charles McDougal, but the amount of energy

948
00:37:26.300 --> 00:37:32.560
and movement that he uses the camera to give this scene of people sitting in a circle,

949
00:37:32.560 --> 00:37:35.720
I mean, it is impressive from a directorial standpoint.

950
00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:43.720
I think, like, I don't want to be crazy, but I think, like, film students should study this portion

951
00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:49.400
of the episode because I'm imagining myself trying to film a group of people sitting in a circle

952
00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:52.260
doing a gift exchange, and it would not look nearly this dynamic.

953
00:37:52.460 --> 00:37:54.020
It's really, really impressive directing.

954
00:37:54.280 --> 00:37:55.240
No, he's great.

955
00:37:55.340 --> 00:37:56.280
He is really great.

956
00:37:56.480 --> 00:37:59.860
Okay, so we're starting the Secret Santa, and Pam opens Jim's teapot.

957
00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:05.060
She loves it, but Dwight moves things along so quickly that she doesn't have time to look inside

958
00:38:05.060 --> 00:38:06.800
or notice the card that's in the box.

959
00:38:06.800 --> 00:38:08.780
Yeah, Dwight wants no chitty chat between gifts.

960
00:38:08.900 --> 00:38:09.740
He's like, go, go, go, go, go.

961
00:38:09.760 --> 00:38:11.080
He's me coming in today.

962
00:38:11.240 --> 00:38:11.680
He is.

963
00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:13.140
He's like, save it for the mic.

964
00:38:13.800 --> 00:38:15.260
So he's moving things along.

965
00:38:15.380 --> 00:38:15.960
So it's Pam.

966
00:38:16.180 --> 00:38:17.260
And then the next one.

967
00:38:17.360 --> 00:38:23.960
We find out that Michael buys Ryan a video iPod that costs $400.

968
00:38:24.740 --> 00:38:26.620
You guys, this was not product placement.

969
00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:27.460
It was not.

970
00:38:27.620 --> 00:38:29.240
So many people wanted to know.

971
00:38:29.420 --> 00:38:31.120
Yeah, we were not paid.

972
00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:34.300
It was just sort of a really cool topical gift at the time.

973
00:38:34.440 --> 00:38:34.620
Yeah.

974
00:38:34.620 --> 00:38:39.100
And they were trying to think of a gift that would sort of be a showstopper that Michael

975
00:38:39.100 --> 00:38:41.780
would think was very impressive, that everyone would want.

976
00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:43.380
So this was coincidence.

977
00:38:43.380 --> 00:38:44.700
We weren't paid to use it.

978
00:38:44.840 --> 00:38:45.880
So I read that.

979
00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:48.040
Well, here's something.

980
00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:51.360
A ton of people wanted to know who kept it at the end.

981
00:38:51.460 --> 00:38:51.720
Nobody.

982
00:38:51.960 --> 00:38:53.600
We weren't allowed to keep any of the stuff.

983
00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:59.500
It all goes into a giant warehouse, and it gets labeled for the episode for props, because

984
00:38:59.980 --> 00:39:03.740
if for some reason we have to go back and reshoot something, they take it off the shelf,

985
00:39:03.740 --> 00:39:04.780
and they bring it back in.

986
00:39:04.920 --> 00:39:05.440
That's true.

987
00:39:05.560 --> 00:39:09.300
I don't know what happens after it's been in the warehouse for a while, but it just goes

988
00:39:09.300 --> 00:39:10.300
to prop house storage.

989
00:39:10.720 --> 00:39:14.260
I feel like it's still in a box labeled the office Christmas party.

990
00:39:14.440 --> 00:39:15.240
It probably is.

991
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:17.780
There was a fan question from Beard Up, Beard Down.

992
00:39:17.960 --> 00:39:19.700
Was the iPod sponsored by Apple?

993
00:39:19.840 --> 00:39:20.500
It wasn't.

994
00:39:20.600 --> 00:39:21.680
We said it was not.

995
00:39:21.880 --> 00:39:23.080
It's just a total coincidence.

996
00:39:23.080 --> 00:39:24.960
But there's more coincidence.

997
00:39:25.880 --> 00:39:32.680
So the week after this episode aired, Apple revealed that you could now download episodes

998
00:39:32.680 --> 00:39:35.380
of The Office onto these video iPods.

999
00:39:35.540 --> 00:39:37.500
Again, this was not planned.

1000
00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:43.420
And then The Office became the number one downloaded show on iTunes.

1001
00:39:43.740 --> 00:39:44.280
Yes.

1002
00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:46.160
The number one downloaded show.

1003
00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:50.520
I remember Rainn Wilson turned to me and said, I think we're going to make it.

1004
00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:52.040
I think we're going to.

1005
00:39:52.180 --> 00:39:56.020
This was the first moment it felt like the tide was turning for us and that we might not

1006
00:39:56.020 --> 00:39:56.660
get canceled.

1007
00:39:56.960 --> 00:39:57.340
All right.

1008
00:39:57.480 --> 00:40:03.480
So next up, Michael gets his gift, the oven mitt knitted by Phyllis.

1009
00:40:03.760 --> 00:40:04.040
Oof.

1010
00:40:04.520 --> 00:40:06.880
Now, everyone had a $20 limit, you guys.

1011
00:40:07.040 --> 00:40:10.980
That's why this iPod really shakes everything up, because he spent $400.

1012
00:40:10.980 --> 00:40:12.380
Yes, yes.

1013
00:40:13.060 --> 00:40:18.520
And he has his line where he says, I only, he says, out in the hallway, he's holding the

1014
00:40:18.520 --> 00:40:20.260
mitt, and he says, do you know what this says?

1015
00:40:20.440 --> 00:40:24.020
This says, I only care about you, a homemade oven mitt's worth.

1016
00:40:24.200 --> 00:40:25.300
He is such a child.

1017
00:40:25.640 --> 00:40:28.000
He is such a bratty kid in this episode.

1018
00:40:28.220 --> 00:40:28.800
Oh, my gosh.

1019
00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:33.480
Well, we had a fan question from Chelsea, Raconza, and Amanda, and many others, actually,

1020
00:40:33.680 --> 00:40:35.740
who actually knitted the oven mitt.

1021
00:40:36.100 --> 00:40:37.440
Well, I asked Phyllis.

1022
00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:39.420
She does not knit in real life.

1023
00:40:39.420 --> 00:40:43.620
Although, she told me that she knitted a scarf for her mom a couple of years ago, but she

1024
00:40:43.620 --> 00:40:44.280
