He had to lay there forever.

1522
01:00:54.780 --> 01:00:58.060
So he laid down on those desks, which were not comfortable, right?

1523
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:59.780
And then they silly stringed his head.

1524
01:01:00.200 --> 01:01:03.400
And then we had all these scenes where that's what he's doing.

1525
01:01:03.560 --> 01:01:07.980
Well, if he got up, all the stuff that he was decorated in would have fallen off.

1526
01:01:07.980 --> 01:01:09.820
It would have been impossible to recreate.

1527
01:01:09.820 --> 01:01:13.200
So he had to just lay there, even when we were on a break.

1528
01:01:13.380 --> 01:01:14.640
Even when we were on a break.

1529
01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:16.020
And he was such a trooper.

1530
01:01:16.160 --> 01:01:16.860
Talk about a trooper.

1531
01:01:17.040 --> 01:01:23.200
And I wrote in my MySpace blog that Kate and I, because Kate and I knew Dave from Improv Days.

1532
01:01:23.260 --> 01:01:25.340
We had all like done improv shows together.

1533
01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:29.620
That Kate and I walked over and talked to him while he had to lay on his back.

1534
01:01:29.900 --> 01:01:33.060
And we just sort of like caught up and that it was so fun to see him.

1535
01:01:33.060 --> 01:01:40.680
But I want you guys to know, if you're wondering what Todd Packer looks like at 20 minutes, 19 seconds, to really paint a picture here.

1536
01:01:40.760 --> 01:01:40.960
Yeah.

1537
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:46.760
He's laying on his back kind of across a desk area partition right in the middle of the room.

1538
01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:54.640
He has blue silly string on his head, Christmas lights around his torso, Christmas garland around his torso,

1539
01:01:55.300 --> 01:02:04.580
Dwight's desk nameplate on his stomach, and there's like a red empty solo cup kind of just like in his, like the crook of his arm.

1540
01:02:04.920 --> 01:02:05.500
You know.

1541
01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:08.800
And he had to lay like that with all those things on top of him.

1542
01:02:08.940 --> 01:02:11.580
He passes out so quickly.

1543
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:15.140
You have to imagine he showed up already half drunk.

1544
01:02:15.340 --> 01:02:16.260
You know he did.

1545
01:02:16.260 --> 01:02:17.020
You know he did.

1546
01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:17.900
You know he did.

1547
01:02:17.900 --> 01:02:26.060
Okay, guys, so now we have the scene where Pam reveals to Jim that she got her teapot back.

1548
01:02:26.680 --> 01:02:33.580
She trades Dwight the iPod for the teapot, and now she's going to look inside and find all the iteMs.

1549
01:02:33.600 --> 01:02:36.740
And it's very charming and sweet, and she is so delighted.

1550
01:02:36.980 --> 01:02:42.420
But in this moment, Jim secretly steals the note back and puts it in his pocket.

1551
01:02:42.640 --> 01:02:43.300
I know.

1552
01:02:43.300 --> 01:02:44.800
He lost his courage.

1553
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:45.740
He did.

1554
01:02:45.740 --> 01:02:53.100
Now, when we reached out to fans to ask them what they wanted to know about the Christmas episode,

1555
01:02:53.340 --> 01:03:00.620
I would say that about 80% of the comments and emails we received were along the lines of,

1556
01:03:00.960 --> 01:03:02.820
what is in the teapot note?

1557
01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:06.600
Because as you know, in this episode, Pam does not read it.

1558
01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:07.640
It is not revealed.

1559
01:03:07.640 --> 01:03:16.300
But then, in season nine, there's a scene where Jim has the documentary film crew put together footage of their romance,

1560
01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:22.260
and he shows it to Pam, and Pam sees that there was a note that Jim steals back,

1561
01:03:22.420 --> 01:03:25.800
and then he hands it to her, and she reads it.

1562
01:03:25.920 --> 01:03:27.120
How brilliant is that?

1563
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:28.200
And you know who that is?

1564
01:03:28.240 --> 01:03:29.240
That's Greg Daniels.

1565
01:03:29.320 --> 01:03:29.480
Yeah.

1566
01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:33.900
Because he was such a master at beautiful callback moments.

1567
01:03:34.520 --> 01:03:35.660
I love that.

1568
01:03:35.800 --> 01:03:39.480
Well, from the time that Jim stole the note, it drove people crazy.

1569
01:03:39.780 --> 01:03:43.020
They always wanted to know what had been written in the note.

1570
01:03:43.220 --> 01:03:44.700
Would Pam ever get the note?

1571
01:03:44.860 --> 01:03:47.540
For years and years, will he ever give her the note?

1572
01:03:47.840 --> 01:03:51.320
Around the time of the wedding, people wanted him to give it to her as a wedding gift.

1573
01:03:52.000 --> 01:03:53.600
Greg saved it till the end.

1574
01:03:53.600 --> 01:03:59.380
And if I'm going to say something that I've never said before, I also feel like I'm maybe going to cry.

1575
01:03:59.820 --> 01:04:00.340
What?

1576
01:04:00.600 --> 01:04:01.060
Wait.

1577
01:04:01.540 --> 01:04:02.060
Wait.

1578
01:04:02.360 --> 01:04:02.740
What?

1579
01:04:03.400 --> 01:04:06.300
Are you going to say what was in the note?

1580
01:04:06.820 --> 01:04:08.500
Are you going to say what was in the note?

1581
01:04:09.780 --> 01:04:10.580
Sort of.

1582
01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:13.560
Because I don't know what was on that card.

1583
01:04:13.800 --> 01:04:14.640
None of us do.

1584
01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:17.600
I'm the only one who knows, and John knows.

1585
01:04:18.060 --> 01:04:19.620
Oh my gosh, lady.

1586
01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:38.060
In that episode in Season 9, I believe Greg suggested to John that he write a personal message from himself to me, just saying what our time together on The Office meant to him.

1587
01:04:38.160 --> 01:04:38.920
Oh, Jenna.

1588
01:04:40.320 --> 01:04:41.980
Because we were wrapping up filming.

1589
01:04:42.120 --> 01:04:45.920
We were wrapping up the series, and we were all so emotional at that time, you know?

1590
01:04:46.260 --> 01:04:49.520
We were all sort of saying goodbye in different ways.

1591
01:04:49.620 --> 01:04:50.020
We were.

1592
01:04:50.020 --> 01:04:53.320
And so that was his goodbye.

1593
01:04:54.460 --> 01:05:05.740
Very similar to when we filmed that scene with Steve, where I said goodbye to him at the airport, and Paul Feig told me, just run up and say goodbye to your friend Steve.

1594
01:05:06.520 --> 01:05:13.580
Jeff Blitz said the same thing to me when I was in the car with Oscar, and I say I love Dwight.

1595
01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:22.980
He said, Angela, in this moment, express your love for the show and everyone, and if you couldn't have it in your life anymore.

1596
01:05:24.040 --> 01:05:25.460
And I disintegrated.

1597
01:05:25.720 --> 01:05:25.880
Yeah.

1598
01:05:26.780 --> 01:05:33.940
So I'm on camera, and I open up this note that John's written me, and I just start crying.

1599
01:05:34.240 --> 01:05:35.400
I just start bawling.

1600
01:05:35.660 --> 01:05:37.760
It probably, the first take was probably not usable.

1601
01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:41.580
It was the sweetest note.

1602
01:05:41.760 --> 01:05:48.800
And you know, on camera, Pam says, I'll never say what it said, but just know it was perfect.

1603
01:05:50.140 --> 01:05:55.500
Well, I'll never say exactly what John wrote, but I will say just know it was perfect.

1604
01:05:55.500 --> 01:05:55.560
Perfect.

1605
01:05:56.840 --> 01:05:58.920
So that's what was in the teapot note, guys.

1606
01:05:59.080 --> 01:06:01.180
It was a note from John to me.

1607
01:06:01.340 --> 01:06:04.820
A personal note about what it meant to work with you on the show.

1608
01:06:04.940 --> 01:06:05.180
Yeah.

1609
01:06:05.380 --> 01:06:05.680
Yeah.

1610
01:06:05.820 --> 01:06:07.680
About our time together on the show, and it was really sweet.

1611
01:06:07.900 --> 01:06:10.600
Well, that would completely wreck me.

1612
01:06:10.920 --> 01:06:11.300
Yeah.

1613
01:06:11.980 --> 01:06:13.400
Oh, I love that.

1614
01:06:13.540 --> 01:06:14.500
I didn't know that.

1615
01:06:14.600 --> 01:06:15.180
Are you okay?

1616
01:06:15.540 --> 01:06:15.980
Yeah.

1617
01:06:16.200 --> 01:06:16.660
Well, crap.

1618
01:06:16.660 --> 01:06:18.100
How do we talk about anything else?

1619
01:06:18.100 --> 01:06:19.280
That was so beautiful.

1620
01:06:19.840 --> 01:06:20.140
I'm sorry.

1621
01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:21.520
That was so beautiful.

1622
01:06:21.520 --> 01:06:24.400
I love that that was the direction that Greg gave.

1623
01:06:24.400 --> 01:06:29.480
Those moments became very honest for us under that kind of direction.

1624
01:06:30.340 --> 01:06:32.640
And we all had little moments like that.

1625
01:06:32.740 --> 01:06:33.980
That's a really big one, though.

1626
01:06:34.180 --> 01:06:36.860
Well, there were those moments on the show that were surprises.

1627
01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:37.500
Yeah.

1628
01:06:37.660 --> 01:06:43.380
Steve didn't know I was going to run up and tell him that basically that same thing.

1629
01:06:43.760 --> 01:06:45.600
Steve, I'm going to miss you.

1630
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:47.280
You know, all the things that I said to him.

1631
01:06:47.560 --> 01:06:49.880
Oscar didn't know the note that Jeff Blitz gave me.

1632
01:06:49.960 --> 01:06:50.100
Yeah.

1633
01:06:50.100 --> 01:06:55.700
So when all that emotion came, it was very, like, completely out of nowhere for him.

1634
01:06:55.880 --> 01:06:56.040
Yeah.

1635
01:06:56.500 --> 01:06:56.860
Okay.

1636
01:06:57.060 --> 01:06:58.840
Well, geez, Louise.

1637
01:06:59.340 --> 01:07:00.000
I'm sorry.

1638
01:07:00.020 --> 01:07:00.760
That's okay.

1639
01:07:00.880 --> 01:07:02.580
Where are we at in this episode?

1640
01:07:03.060 --> 01:07:08.200
Well, we're at the moment when Kelly approaches Dwight in the kitchen.

1641
01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:09.580
Kelly, that hussy.

1642
01:07:09.740 --> 01:07:12.180
Oh, with her hair half down, half up.

1643
01:07:12.240 --> 01:07:13.000
I know.

1644
01:07:13.160 --> 01:07:16.380
She goes up to my man and lays one on him.

1645
01:07:16.380 --> 01:07:16.960
She does.

1646
01:07:16.960 --> 01:07:17.160
Yes.

1647
01:07:17.380 --> 01:07:21.140
And Angela sees it, and that is it.

1648
01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:28.000
You know, a lot of people wrote in and commented that you're standing in front of a poster that

1649
01:07:28.000 --> 01:07:28.820
says commitment.

1650
01:07:29.300 --> 01:07:29.940
Am I really?

1651
01:07:30.160 --> 01:07:30.380
Yes.

1652
01:07:30.460 --> 01:07:30.940
Oh, my gosh.

1653
01:07:30.940 --> 01:07:31.860
I didn't even notice.

1654
01:07:32.140 --> 01:07:33.160
That is so funny.

1655
01:07:33.280 --> 01:07:35.120
I think I was just so focused on the scene.

1656
01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:35.420
Yeah.

1657
01:07:35.420 --> 01:07:36.200
Wow.

1658
01:07:36.620 --> 01:07:36.920
Yes.

1659
01:07:37.180 --> 01:07:38.960
Angela loses it.

1660
01:07:39.440 --> 01:07:40.240
Loses it.

1661
01:07:40.420 --> 01:07:42.420
And this takes us outside.

1662
01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:47.240
She's left the party, and now I have some stuff to tell you guys about this scene.

1663
01:07:47.360 --> 01:07:47.410
Oh, yeah.

1664
01:07:48.020 --> 01:07:48.500
All right.

1665
01:07:48.740 --> 01:07:50.240
20 minutes, 16 seconds.

1666
01:07:50.540 --> 01:07:52.900
The ultimate Angela pissed-offness has happened.

1667
01:07:53.400 --> 01:07:55.240
So here's some behind the scenes of this scene.

1668
01:07:55.740 --> 01:07:59.620
You have a guy up on the roof, and he's got the soap snow.

1669
01:07:59.940 --> 01:08:00.220
Yep.

1670
01:08:00.320 --> 01:08:00.920
That he's going to-

1671
01:08:00.920 --> 01:08:01.880
Falling into your eyes.

1672
01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:03.800
He's going to, yeah, stinging.

1673
01:08:04.740 --> 01:08:08.360
And then there's snow on the ground, because they've put real snow on the ground.

1674
01:08:08.700 --> 01:08:11.520
We filmed this scene at the end of the day, and everyone had gone.

1675
01:08:11.960 --> 01:08:15.900
It was just me and Charles McDougal, Randall Einhorn, and Mike Schur.

1676
01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:18.120
So it was just a kind of a skeleton crew at this point.

1677
01:08:18.220 --> 01:08:20.080
Those are always some of my most favorite shoots.

1678
01:08:20.380 --> 01:08:21.260
Yeah, me too.

1679
01:08:21.380 --> 01:08:23.320
And we did not have a lot of time.

1680
01:08:23.740 --> 01:08:25.160
We didn't have a lot of time to get this.

1681
01:08:25.160 --> 01:08:26.040
Oh, the clock was ticking.

1682
01:08:26.320 --> 01:08:30.380
Yeah, exactly, because we didn't want to go into overtime for everyone, and it was the end

1683
01:08:30.380 --> 01:08:30.860
of the day.

1684
01:08:30.860 --> 01:08:37.280
And so Charles McDougal said to me, we're probably only going to do like two takes, maybe three.

1685
01:08:37.480 --> 01:08:44.940
But they gave me these ornaments, and my instruction was that my character has just lost it.

1686
01:08:45.040 --> 01:08:46.800
Michael has ruined Christmas.

1687
01:08:47.360 --> 01:08:49.140
Kelly has kissed my man.

1688
01:08:49.380 --> 01:08:51.940
Ryan is the king of the party planning committee.

1689
01:08:52.780 --> 01:08:53.300
Right?

1690
01:08:53.540 --> 01:08:53.800
Yes.

1691
01:08:53.900 --> 01:08:57.840
He said, I want you to take these ornaments and just throw them and shatter them.

1692
01:08:57.840 --> 01:09:00.660
They were written in the script as glass ornaments.

1693
01:09:01.360 --> 01:09:03.040
They were not glass ornaments.

1694
01:09:03.340 --> 01:09:03.560
What?

1695
01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:04.640
Watch the scene.

1696
01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:05.400
I throw them down.

1697
01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:07.680
They bounce straight up in the air.

1698
01:09:07.840 --> 01:09:08.620
What were they?

1699
01:09:08.760 --> 01:09:11.640
They were like some kind of plastic composite whatever.

1700
01:09:12.020 --> 01:09:12.660
Oh, no.

1701
01:09:12.960 --> 01:09:14.820
So when you look, watch it, you guys.

1702
01:09:14.920 --> 01:09:16.420
You see them bounce in the air.

1703
01:09:16.760 --> 01:09:19.140
I assumed, well, that makes sense.

1704
01:09:19.140 --> 01:09:24.640
We did not have the budget to get special breakaway glass ornaments, and there's no way

1705
01:09:24.640 --> 01:09:26.160
they would give you real glass.

1706
01:09:26.400 --> 01:09:26.620
No.

1707
01:09:26.880 --> 01:09:29.900
So these things bounced like a tennis ball.

1708
01:09:30.320 --> 01:09:32.240
And so Charles is like, cut.

1709
01:09:32.380 --> 01:09:33.980
And he goes, okay, two things.

1710
01:09:34.200 --> 01:09:36.780
One, we need you to stand closer to the wall.

1711
01:09:36.900 --> 01:09:40.300
Like, if you can in the scene, get as close to the wall as possible, because that's where

1712
01:09:40.300 --> 01:09:42.860
the guy is with the soap coming down.

1713
01:09:43.060 --> 01:09:44.760
The soap doesn't ball very far.

1714
01:09:44.920 --> 01:09:48.980
So we have another take, and he's like, why aren't you breaking the ornaments?

1715
01:09:49.120 --> 01:09:50.120
I'm like, Charles, they're bouncing.

1716
01:09:50.120 --> 01:09:50.940
What are you talking about?

1717
01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:52.200
He goes, can you throw them harder?

1718
01:09:52.320 --> 01:09:54.000
I was like, yeah, they're just going to bounce higher.

1719
01:09:54.700 --> 01:09:56.460
And I was like, okay, I got it.

1720
01:09:56.520 --> 01:09:56.820
I got it.

1721
01:09:56.840 --> 01:09:57.440
I have an idea.

1722
01:09:58.540 --> 01:10:00.960
So I know now we're really running out of time.

1723
01:10:01.340 --> 01:10:07.600
So, and Michael Gallenberg had taken the most awesome photo that I have, and it's the snow

1724
01:10:07.600 --> 01:10:12.620
falling and me throwing the ornaments and Charles McDougal in the distance watching me.

1725
01:10:13.000 --> 01:10:14.320
Oh, that's great.

1726
01:10:14.440 --> 01:10:16.180
Michael Gallenberg, our set designer.

1727
01:10:16.300 --> 01:10:17.360
Yeah, he took this photo.

1728
01:10:17.500 --> 01:10:18.020
It was so cool.

1729
01:10:18.160 --> 01:10:19.480
But anyway, here I am.

1730
01:10:19.680 --> 01:10:20.580
We're running out of time.

1731
01:10:20.800 --> 01:10:21.520
I got to stand.

1732
01:10:21.640 --> 01:10:22.880
I got to get myself to the wall.

1733
01:10:22.880 --> 01:10:27.500
I got to throw these ornaments, and I need them to break, and I have to shriek, right?

1734
01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:30.820
So I throw them with, I said, I'm going to throw them harder this time.

1735
01:10:30.820 --> 01:10:31.280
I don't know.

1736
01:10:31.420 --> 01:10:32.900
So I threw them as hard as I could.

1737
01:10:33.580 --> 01:10:34.740
They bounced up higher.

1738
01:10:35.640 --> 01:10:40.580
I shrieked, and I just started stomping on them and shattering them with my feet.

1739
01:10:40.700 --> 01:10:44.060
Was that your intention going in when you're like, I have an idea.

1740
01:10:44.060 --> 01:10:44.580
I can do it.

1741
01:10:44.620 --> 01:10:44.900
I can do it.

1742
01:10:44.900 --> 01:10:48.180
I was thinking if I can't get them to break, I have to start stomping on them.

1743
01:10:48.220 --> 01:10:48.540
Yes.

1744
01:10:48.540 --> 01:10:49.820
So that's what I just did.

1745
01:10:49.920 --> 01:10:51.100
That was just an improv in the moment.

1746
01:10:51.220 --> 01:10:52.320
I just started stomping on them.

1747
01:10:52.680 --> 01:10:54.860
Folks, notice I'm wearing my Sass shoes.

1748
01:10:55.140 --> 01:10:57.280
Oh, that's the perfect shoe for this.

1749
01:10:57.320 --> 01:10:58.040
I know.

1750
01:10:58.240 --> 01:10:59.360
And so I shriek.

1751
01:10:59.480 --> 01:11:00.360
I get to the wall.

1752
01:11:00.480 --> 01:11:01.400
I'm stomping things.

1753
01:11:01.500 --> 01:11:02.740
I rip the box apart.

1754
01:11:03.300 --> 01:11:04.400
We got the scene.

1755
01:11:04.960 --> 01:11:05.260
Oh.

1756
01:11:05.680 --> 01:11:10.680
Let me tell you, ToneLoke89 is going to be very happy because they wrote in with a fan

1757
01:11:10.680 --> 01:11:11.160
question.

1758
01:11:11.360 --> 01:11:12.000
What was that?

1759
01:11:12.160 --> 01:11:16.040
One of my favorite scenes is when Angela screams and smashes the glass ornaments.

1760
01:11:16.040 --> 01:11:18.000
What was it like to film?

1761
01:11:18.420 --> 01:11:19.320
All of that.

1762
01:11:19.540 --> 01:11:20.560
Yes, exactly.

1763
01:11:20.920 --> 01:11:24.980
But now if you go back and watch the scene, you guys watch like the first two that I throw.

1764
01:11:25.260 --> 01:11:27.020
I think that's kind of from the first take.

1765
01:11:27.220 --> 01:11:28.380
They bounce straight up.

1766
01:11:28.960 --> 01:11:33.020
So when we go back up in the office, I have to point out that when everybody decides to go

1767
01:11:33.020 --> 01:11:37.180
to poor Richard's, Michael gets invited and the look on his face.

1768
