1823
01:13:57.460 --> 01:13:58.380
Oh, well, there you go.

1824
01:13:58.380 --> 01:13:58.580
So there you go.

1825
01:13:58.780 --> 01:13:59.960
They were right there together.

1826
01:14:00.160 --> 01:14:02.620
And Kevin has a whole rap.

1827
01:14:02.860 --> 01:14:04.080
He raps.

1828
01:14:04.520 --> 01:14:05.000
Oh!

1829
01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:06.740
A whole portion of a song.

1830
01:14:06.960 --> 01:14:09.700
So really check out these deleted scenes if you can.

1831
01:14:09.840 --> 01:14:10.740
They're fantastic.

1832
01:14:11.160 --> 01:14:11.360
All right.

1833
01:14:11.440 --> 01:14:13.780
Let's talk about the final scene inside The Office.

1834
01:14:14.140 --> 01:14:14.600
All right.

1835
01:14:14.720 --> 01:14:16.080
It happens in Michael's office.

1836
01:14:16.420 --> 01:14:17.440
He's getting ready to leave.

1837
01:14:17.600 --> 01:14:18.420
He's going to go downstairs.

1838
01:14:19.640 --> 01:14:29.300
Meredith just walks into his office, takes off her top, and then Steve, as Michael, takes

1839
01:14:29.300 --> 01:14:30.920
a picture and then walks out.

1840
01:14:31.100 --> 01:14:32.420
I have a fan question.

1841
01:14:32.420 --> 01:14:36.900
Well, first of all, Kate, I really wanted Kate to be able to call in for this one.

1842
01:14:37.080 --> 01:14:40.940
I traded texts with her, but she is starting a tour with Dancing with the Stars.

1843
01:14:41.160 --> 01:14:41.540
Oh, yeah.

1844
01:14:41.660 --> 01:14:42.660
And she's traveling today.

1845
01:14:42.800 --> 01:14:43.620
She's on a plane.

1846
01:14:43.760 --> 01:14:45.340
And she called me night before laSt.

1847
01:14:45.400 --> 01:14:47.660
And she was like, Ange, I'm so sorry I can't come in.

1848
01:14:47.800 --> 01:14:52.300
But she was like, I really do want to come in and talk about all things Meredith.

1849
01:14:52.540 --> 01:14:53.780
So she will come eventually.

1850
01:14:54.080 --> 01:14:54.800
Oh, that's good.

1851
01:14:54.800 --> 01:14:58.140
I have a feeling you might know the answer to this fan question.

1852
01:14:58.420 --> 01:14:58.540
Okay.

1853
01:14:59.260 --> 01:15:05.560
Carrie Schaub said, or maybe it's Carrie Shabe, said, when characters flash each other, are

1854
01:15:05.560 --> 01:15:08.380
the actors really flashing each other in real life?

1855
01:15:08.620 --> 01:15:09.640
No, no, no.

1856
01:15:09.780 --> 01:15:10.080
No.

1857
01:15:10.280 --> 01:15:10.540
No.

1858
01:15:10.760 --> 01:15:11.780
I mean, sort of.

1859
01:15:11.880 --> 01:15:12.120
Sort of.

1860
01:15:12.280 --> 01:15:12.460
But no.

1861
01:15:12.620 --> 01:15:14.500
I mean, it's still embarrassing.

1862
01:15:15.040 --> 01:15:20.020
Even if I had to, like, be in a bathing suit, I'd feel awkward.

1863
01:15:20.180 --> 01:15:20.660
You know what I mean?

1864
01:15:20.760 --> 01:15:22.020
Kate was wearing pasties.

1865
01:15:22.180 --> 01:15:22.940
Kate had things.

1866
01:15:22.940 --> 01:15:23.980
She was kind of covered.

1867
01:15:24.140 --> 01:15:24.240
Yeah.

1868
01:15:24.380 --> 01:15:25.980
She had things over her hoo-hahs.

1869
01:15:26.160 --> 01:15:26.300
Yeah.

1870
01:15:26.580 --> 01:15:27.700
Steve is such a gentleman.

1871
01:15:27.900 --> 01:15:29.880
He said, Kate, I'm just going to look at, like, your neck.

1872
01:15:30.140 --> 01:15:30.460
Yeah.

1873
01:15:31.040 --> 01:15:32.280
Stare at your clavicle.

1874
01:15:32.520 --> 01:15:34.380
They had no crew inside.

1875
01:15:34.640 --> 01:15:34.760
Yep.

1876
01:15:34.900 --> 01:15:37.220
Her image wasn't on any monitors anywhere.

1877
01:15:37.560 --> 01:15:38.000
That's right.

1878
01:15:38.000 --> 01:15:40.620
And there was no chip in the digital camera.

1879
01:15:40.900 --> 01:15:42.400
So the flash goes off.

1880
01:15:42.400 --> 01:15:43.960
It looks like Michael's taking a picture.

1881
01:15:44.120 --> 01:15:46.440
But there was actually never a picture taken.

1882
01:15:46.720 --> 01:15:47.080
Never a photo.

1883
01:15:47.240 --> 01:15:52.380
So they were very, very mindful of taking care of Kate in that moment.

1884
01:15:52.940 --> 01:15:56.900
Kate would go on as Meredith to take off her clothes.

1885
01:15:57.260 --> 01:15:57.960
Quite a bit.

1886
01:15:58.060 --> 01:15:58.520
Quite a bit.

1887
01:15:58.840 --> 01:16:04.240
One of my favorite things is that Kate's father wrote her a handwritten letter.

1888
01:16:04.520 --> 01:16:05.420
Oh, my goodness.

1889
01:16:05.820 --> 01:16:10.420
And all it said, this is her father, who, you know, Kate is from Pennsylvania.

1890
01:16:10.420 --> 01:16:15.940
And all it said was, dear Kate, stop taking your clothes off.

1891
01:16:16.240 --> 01:16:17.180
Love, dad.

1892
01:16:17.440 --> 01:16:18.620
Oh, my gosh.

1893
01:16:19.780 --> 01:16:20.980
Oh, my gosh.

1894
01:16:21.960 --> 01:16:23.580
What did Kate do?

1895
01:16:23.740 --> 01:16:24.920
How did she respond to that?

1896
01:16:24.940 --> 01:16:26.260
She was like, oh, man.

1897
01:16:26.680 --> 01:16:29.160
Now, is that her dad having a sense of humor?

1898
01:16:29.160 --> 01:16:31.760
Or is that him being like, seriously, stop it?

1899
01:16:31.940 --> 01:16:32.700
I think both.

1900
01:16:32.880 --> 01:16:33.440
I think both.

1901
01:16:33.440 --> 01:16:33.920
All right.

1902
01:16:34.060 --> 01:16:35.520
Should we talk about the parking lot?

1903
01:16:35.760 --> 01:16:37.240
We're almost done here.

1904
01:16:37.820 --> 01:16:38.200
Yes.

1905
01:16:38.360 --> 01:16:39.520
Let's talk about the parking lot.

1906
01:16:39.660 --> 01:16:45.620
Because it is definitely one of the most magical moments that I remember in filming all nine years.

1907
01:16:45.640 --> 01:16:46.980
And we all say that.

1908
01:16:47.240 --> 01:16:47.460
Yeah.

1909
01:16:47.620 --> 01:16:51.020
People often ask, like, what were your favorite scenes?

1910
01:16:51.340 --> 01:16:54.080
And it's always hard to explain.

1911
01:16:54.080 --> 01:16:57.800
Because sometimes your favorite scene, it doesn't seem like that exciting of a scene.

1912
01:16:57.800 --> 01:17:01.280
But it's what happened behind the scenes that make it your favorite.

1913
01:17:01.440 --> 01:17:03.180
And this parking lot scene is one of mine.

1914
01:17:03.800 --> 01:17:04.180
Definitely.

1915
01:17:04.720 --> 01:17:04.980
Definitely.

1916
01:17:05.460 --> 01:17:05.740
Okay.

1917
01:17:05.760 --> 01:17:07.400
So it's the end of the day.

1918
01:17:07.540 --> 01:17:09.780
We have all of this real snow on the ground.

1919
01:17:10.180 --> 01:17:11.680
And everyone is leaving.

1920
01:17:11.680 --> 01:17:13.340
And everyone's in good spirits.

1921
01:17:13.600 --> 01:17:14.820
And it's really nighttime.

1922
01:17:15.180 --> 01:17:17.560
It was rare for us to ever work past 6 p.m.

1923
01:17:17.580 --> 01:17:18.840
So we always got excited.

1924
01:17:19.120 --> 01:17:23.520
To walk out in the dark, I think, we all felt like we were up past our bedtime.

1925
01:17:23.820 --> 01:17:26.300
But also, you have to remember, this is Los Angeles.

1926
01:17:26.300 --> 01:17:28.440
There's never snow on the ground.

1927
01:17:28.660 --> 01:17:33.720
So this is magical in itself that we have a parking lot full of snow.

1928
01:17:34.100 --> 01:17:42.360
And as we're walking to the cars, I don't know, like, the shot you see, I'm actually in the front passenger seat of an SUV.

1929
01:17:42.580 --> 01:17:44.660
But I'm only half in, like, the door's open.

1930
01:17:44.860 --> 01:17:49.340
But I remember one of the guys just picked up some snow and flung it at the other one.

1931
01:17:49.500 --> 01:17:54.720
And then they all started picking up snow and having this impromptu snowball fight.

1932
01:17:54.840 --> 01:17:55.000
Yeah.

1933
01:17:55.000 --> 01:17:56.720
And everyone loved it.

1934
